Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++-v3/configure: recognize substrate for shared lib builds

The libtool host_os case statements that decide "does this OS support
shared libraries via GNU ld" and "what's the dynamic linker on this
host" only list linux* / k*bsd*-gnu / kopensolaris*-gnu / etc.  Without
a matching arm, an i386-unknown-substrate cross build of libstdc++
falls through to the defaults: enable_shared=no, dynamic_linker=no,
and the build produces libstdc++.a only.

Add `substrate*` to those case alternatives so an --enable-shared
configure produces a real ET_DYN libstdc++.so.6 with a SONAME entry
and is recognised as supporting shared libraries.

Note: the libstdc++.so produced by libtool still needs a follow-up
manual relink with -lc -lgcc_s to populate DT_NEEDED entries —
substrate's libtool postdeps for $host_os aren't wired up to add
those automatically yet.  See contrib/gcc/build-libstdcxx-shared.sh
for the helper that does the end-to-end build.

---
 libstdc++-v3/configure | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/configure b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ libstdc++-v3/configure @@
-    gnu* | linux* | tpf* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | uclinuxfdpiceabi)
+    gnu* | linux* | substrate* | tpf* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | uclinuxfdpiceabi)
@@ libstdc++-v3/configure @@
-linux* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu* | uclinuxfdpiceabi)
+linux* | substrate* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu* | uclinuxfdpiceabi)
@@ libstdc++-v3/configure @@
-      gnu* | linux* | kfreebsd*-gnu | knetbsd*-gnu)
+      gnu* | linux* | substrate* | kfreebsd*-gnu | knetbsd*-gnu)
@@ libstdc++-v3/configure @@
-      gnu* | linux* | kfreebsd*-gnu | knetbsd*-gnu | uclinux*)
+      gnu* | linux* | substrate* | kfreebsd*-gnu | knetbsd*-gnu | uclinux*)
@@ libstdc++-v3/configure @@
-      gnu* | linux* | solaris* | uclinux*)
+      gnu* | linux* | substrate* | solaris* | uclinux*)
